 "discrepancies": [
  "Guinea 2025: the USGS estimate of bauxite mined is 150 Mt, 34% of the world total, but Guinea's exports alone were reported at 182.8 Mt for 2025 (Reuters, from official Guinean data (Hellenic Shipping News, 26 January 2026), https://www.hellenicshippingnews.com/guineas-bauxite-exports-jump-25-to-183-million-tons-in-2025-on-chinese-demand/), which is more than USGS estimates it mined. The USGS production figure and Guinea's share of the world total are therefore probably understated."
 ]
